<!--
  Chapter 65 — Performance, Chaos & Architecture Tests.
    load/     LoadModels (closed: looping virtual users; open: requests at a rate, timed from when due), Latencies (with
              coordinated-omission correction), StallingServer (a service that freezes periodically)
    chaos/    FaultProxy (latency, errors, a hung dependency), Services (order-service with three client set-ups),
              Experiment (steady-state hypothesis, fault, abort condition)
    arch/     ClassGraph (dependencies from bytecode, via the JDK's ClassFile API), Rules (layers, cycles, allowed
              dependencies, naming, standard streams), Freeze, FoodFleetRules; sample/ the service they guard
  verify/run.sh runs the load models, the chaos experiment and ten planted architecture violations.
-->
